---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About AmirHossein, nullamix: DevOps engineer focused on Linux, containers, CI/CD, automation, and observability.">
  <article class="article">
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>AmirHossein, aka nullamix.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        DevOps engineer working across Linux, Docker, CI/CD, private registries,
        automation, monitoring, and production troubleshooting.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Focus</h2>
      <p>
        My strongest interests are practical infrastructure engineering: building reliable
        delivery pipelines, hardening container workflows, making internal platforms less fragile,
        and documenting the trade-offs behind engineering decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>Stack I write about</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Linux, networking, Docker, Kubernetes, and container image hardening.</li>
        <li>GitLab CI, GitHub Actions, Ansible, private registries, Nexus, Harbor, and Trivy.</li>
        <li>Zabbix, Prometheus, Grafana, logs, metrics, and incident troubleshooting.</li>
        <li>Python, Bash, Go, and small automation tools that remove operational toil.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Writing rule</h2>
      <p>
        Every post should answer a concrete question, expose the failure mode, and leave behind
        a command, config, or decision framework that another engineer can reuse.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
